  All user stories in the PRD have been completed. Here's a summary of US-010 im
  plementation:

  US-010: Handle Edge Cases and Error Recovery ✅

  Changes Made to src/model/cashu/tx-recovery.ts:

  1. Exponential Backoff Retry (withRetry):
    • 3 max retries with base delay of 1000ms
    • Delay doubles each attempt: 1s, 2s, 4s
    • Applied to all network operations (quote fetching, melts, mints, proof loc
      , publishing)
  2. Quote Expiry Handling:
    • handleQuoteExpiry() - automatically aborts transaction and releases reserv
      roofs
    • Applied in perform_melt and perform_mint steps
    • Checks expiry before operation AND catches expiry errors during execution
  3. Zap Invoice Failure Handling:
    • handleZapInvoiceFailure() - aborts transaction when LNURL fetch fails
    • Applied in fetch_zap_invoice step with retry logic
  4. Mint Error Handling:
    • handleMintError() - aborts transaction and releases funds on any mint oper
      n failure
    • Applied to all mint-related operations
  5. Enhanced Error Detection:
    • Expanded isRetryableError() to detect network, timeout, 503, 429, connecti
      eset errors

  Key Pattern:

  try {
    result = await withRetry(() => mintOperation(), 'operation name');
  } catch (error) {
    if (isQuoteExpiredError(error)) return handleQuoteExpiry(txId, 'mint');
    return handleMintError(txId, error);
  }

  This ensures no funds are ever lost - if anything goes wrong, the transaction
  is automatically aborted and reserved proofs are returned to the wallet.
